{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258908,"nonce":"xjIWDG6qcdyxRToPvuvL2nQi4rY=","title":"bench_method_call: the accumulated field is loaded and stored every iteration of the OSR loop","message":"With the zero-divisor arm gone from `Acc.step` (`self.total = self.total + (i % 8)`), the OSR resume function for main's loop is a load, an and, an add and a store per iteration, with no call and no pending check left (ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR, fn-main_resume0-tier1.hir). The field is never kept in a register across iterations, so the loop runs at store-forwarding latency: whole-process wall on the NUC is about 0.26 s both before and after removing the check, PyPy about 0.09 to 0.15 s.\n\nThe field's address is a live-in of the resume function (`*%Acc` argument), so a promotion of the load and store out of the loop has to show the store runs on every iteration, or that the object does not escape to another thread. Either the HIR LICM could promote a field of a pointer the loop body only reads and writes through itself, or the LLVM tier's function could carry what makes LLVM's own promotion fire (a rotated loop, noalias or dereferenceable on the live-in).","files":null}]}